From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:22:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: macsmc: report the SMC's input interrupts

The SMC can watch an input and report its configured level or edge as an
event of type 0x7202, with the line number in bits 15:8; it holds the next
event for that line until the line is acknowledged with command 5. The
driver defined the commands (IRQ enable 4, ack 5, mode 6) but never used
them, so no SMC input could be an interrupt. The earlier Asahi Linux
version of this driver had the support; this brings it back in the
current driver's shape:

- Only a node marked interrupt-controller gets an irqchip, so no other
  Mac changes. Lines whose IRQ mode reads back at probe are the ones that
  can interrupt.
- Events come from the SMC's notifier chain in process context, so the
  lines are nested threaded interrupts. Every handled event is
  acknowledged on its own key, whether or not a consumer mapped the line,
  or the SMC would hold the next one.
- The irqchip callbacks only record the wanted mode and enable; the bus
  unlock writes each of them only when it differs from what the SMC was
  last given, and a failed write is retried at the next unlock. The
  earlier version copied the mode the wrong way after a write, which wrote
  it again at every unlock.
- The chip is immutable and uses the gpiolib resource helpers.

tools/asahi/macsmc-gpio-irq-tests.py builds the event handler and the
irqchip callbacks from this file against a fixture that records every SMC
write and nested interrupt (8 cases), and kills three mutations: no ack,
the earlier mode bookkeeping, and an unchecked event type.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpio/Kconfig                 |   1 +
 drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c           | 217 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tools/asahi/macsmc-gpio-irq-tests.py | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/asahi/run-host-tests.py        |   3 +
 4 files changed, 443 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tools/asahi/macsmc-gpio-irq-tests.py

